 "is_vocab": false,
 "stimulus_html": "For the following exercises, use the graph shown.\n<br>\n<img src=\"exercises/media/1395c70ed94072d2.png\" alt=\"A line is plotted on an x y coordinate plane. The x and y axes range from negative 10 to 10, in increments of 1. The line passes through the points, (negative 3, negative 7), (negative 1, 1), (0, 5), and (1, 9). Note: all values are approximate.\">\n",
 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 511349,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "True or False. This graph has a slope of 5.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1000624,
     "content_html": "True",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 1000625,
     "content_html": "False",
     "correctness": "1.0"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "true-false"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "Count the rise over run between the two labeled points. The rise is 4. The run is 1. The rise over run is 4, not 5."
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "False"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  },
  {
   "id": 511350,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "True or False. This is the graph of the equation <span data-math=\"y = {\\text{ }}4x + 5\">y = {\\text{ }}4x + 5</span> .",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1000626,
     "content_html": "True",
     "correctness": "1.0"
    },
    {
     "id": 1000627,
     "content_html": "False",
     "correctness": "0.0"
    }
   ],
   "hints": [],
   "formats": [
    "true-false"
   ],
   "combo_choices": [],
   "collaborator_solutions": [
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>The slope is 4. The <i>y-</i>intercept is (0, 5).</p>\n<p>When the equation is in the slope-intercept form of the equation of the line,</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"y = mx + b\"></span>.</p>\n<p><i>m</i> = the slope.</p>\n<p>(0, <i>b</i>) = the y-intercept.</p>\n<p>This line is <span data-math=\"y = 4x + 5\"></span>.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "True"
    }
   ],
   "community_solutions": []
  }
 ],
